ng Dong-ho","aliases":["Kang Dong-ho"],"birth":"1995-07-21","death":"","birthplace":"Jeju Province","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q225105","name":"NU'EST","start":"2012","end":"2022"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/realbaekho/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/2c247ad9-9737-49eb-a78e-0954d4a579fb"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/160312_baekho.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:160312_baekho.jpg","author":"147company","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kang Dong-ho, known professionally as Baekho (백호), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, record producer, and musical theatre actor. Formerly the main vocalist and music producer of South Korean boy group NU'EST, Baekho made his debut as a solo artist in October 2022 with the release of his first extended play Absolute Zero. Known for his powerhouse vocals and powerful physique, he has been dubbed the \"Sexy Icon\" of his generation.","title":"Baekho (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baekho_%28singer%29"}},"Q30337148":{"id":"Q30337148","name":"Kim So-hee","ko":"김소희","birthName":"김소희","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Sohee"],"birth":"1999-12-31","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2017","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q30036738","name":"Alice","start":"2017","end":"2024"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/s2k1m/","x":"https://x.com/iok_alice","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3mYdRRihv7Oj0g4a7viHOX","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/2d33c7d6-e349-44e7-aff8-36f746d1492e"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim So-hee is a South Korean former singer. She is known for being a contestant of K-pop Star 6: The Last Chance, in which she emerged as runner-up as a member of KWINs. She debuted as a solo artist on May 21, 2017 and on June 1, 2017, she debuted as a member of Alice. On April 26, 2024, Sohee left Alice and retired from the entertainment industry.","title":"Kim So-hee (singer, born 1999)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_So-hee_%28singer%2C_born_1999%29"}},"Q30921468":{"id":"Q30921468","name":"Kwon Chae-won","ko":"권채원","birthName":"권채원","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Eunchae"],"birth":"1999-05-26","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"MBK Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q429296","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20733515","name":"DIA","start":"2016","end":"2022"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/silver_chae_526/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/b2c7d32a-e176-4c4d-bd2e-28239d33b80b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kwon Chae-won, previously known as Eunchae, is a South Korean singer and actress. She is a member of girl group DIA. Apart from her group's activities, Kwon has also starred in Tooniverse's first web drama The Shining Nara, which has gained popularity with over 10 million views in the first month on YouTube.","title":"Kwon Chae-won","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwon_Chae-won"}},"Q491580":{"id":"Q491580","name":"Eric Mun","ko":"문정혁","birthName":"문정혁","birthNameEn":"Mun Jung-hyuk","aliases":["Mun Jung-hyuk","Mun Jeonghyeok"],"birth":"1979-02-16","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","actor"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"1998","end":"2003"},{"name":"Good Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q10855622","start":"2003","end":"2008"},{"name":"Shinhwa Company","korean":false,"id":"Q20023037","start":"2011","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q482620","name":"Shinhwa","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ericofficial__/","x":"https://x.com/ej_ent","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCrufTWlMgYEK71hSyJcR5Ng","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/3ec4c81e-c177-4430-beb8-3779e7cd7a7e"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Eric Mun, birth name Mun Jung-hyuk (Korean: 문정혁, is a South Korean rapper, songwriter and actor. He is a member and leader of the South Korean boy band Shinhwa. He is also well known for several dramas such as Phoenix (2004), Super Rookie (2005), and Another Oh Hae-young (2016). He was with Top Class Entertainment from 2007 to December 2013. In 2014, Mun and his manager of 10 years, Lee Jong-hyun, set up a new management agency, E&J Entertainment, for his individual activities. Mun is also the CEO of Shinhwa Company, the home agency of his group, with Lee Min-woo as co-CEO since 2011, and with the remaining members—Kim Dong-wan, Shin Hye-sung, Jun Jin and Andy Lee—as shareholders.","title":"Eric Mun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Mun"}},"Q498044":{"id":"Q498044","name":"Kim Bo-kyeong","ko":"김보경","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Bo-kyung"],"birth":"1990-05-16","death":"","birthplace":"Asan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2010","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/sssbkkk/","x":"https://x.com/sssbkkk","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9ec375a1-de2b-4df4-ba72-4cadeca77163"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q498364":{"id":"Q498364","name":"Lee Ji-hyun","ko":"이지현","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Ji Hyun","Lee Jihyun"],"birth":"1983-10-12","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer"],"debut":"2001","agencies":[{"name":"Star Empire Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q3206859","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q490873","name":"Jewelry","start":"2001","end":"2006"}],"links":{"instagram"